# {{party}}/{{name}}

A Kontra offering: a durable, quoted job that buyers hire through Kontra and that runs on
your own machine as a Temporal worker. Made by `kontra init`.

| File | Owner of |
|---|---|
| `offering.yaml` | name, version, limits, display text: declarative, no code names |
| `models.py` | the input and output types; the published contract is derived from them |
| `workflows.py`, `activities.py` | the job itself: Temporal, imported only through `kontra` (`from kontra import workflow, activity`) |
| `quote.py` | the price, from the input |
| `worker.py` | `serve({{Class}}Flow, ...)`: the binding of workflow and quote to the offering, and all worker tuning |
| `tests/test_offering.py` | the whole lifecycle (quote, hire, deliver, accept; a refund) with no containers |

## Try it locally

```sh
kontra dev                                    # a local Kontra in Docker, with play money
kontra serve                                  # serve this offering (a dev profile publishes it)
kontra quote {{party}}/{{name}} -f input.json
kontra hire {{party}}/{{name}} -f input.json --max-price 1 --wait --accept
```

## Test it

```sh
pip install "kontra-sdk[testing]" pytest
pytest
```

## Sell it

```sh
kontra login
kontra publish        # needs a recent login; prints the contract hash and the endpoint
kontra serve          # on the machine that does the work
```

A published version is fixed. Change the types in `models.py` or anything in
`offering.yaml`, and bump `version` before publishing again: `kontra serve` refuses to serve
code whose contract differs from the catalog's.
